<title>JAPAN: Toray says rate of 120 yen/$ best for its business.</title>
<headline>Toray says rate of 120 yen/$ best for its business.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese maker of synthetic fibres Toray Industries Inc said on Thursday that a rate of 120 yen to the dollar was the most comfortable level for the company's exports and imports.</p>
<p>Company president Katsuhiko Hirai told a luncheon with foreign journalists that he was eager to see stable currencies, adding that &quot;it was most troublesome&quot; to see currencies moving wildly in the aftermath of verbal intervention by government officials.</p>
</text>
